<http://data.silknow.org/object/c4076c8a-87e1-3cef-99ea-a0c97c48d577>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Embroidered chair seat, England, ca. 1730."@en , "Chair seat canvas, embroidered with wool and silk in shades of mustard, red, pink, green, blue, grey, beige, mauve, brown, cream, and yellow.\nThe border has a mustard-coloured ground and is decorated with large, brightly-coloured flowers; carnation, lily, convolvulus and peony.\nThe central embroidered scene of 'The Father and Jupiter' is taken from William Kent's illustration to the 39th of Gay's Fables. The initials 'E.W.' are embroidered on a plinth in the foreground of the scene."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/036443f9-9931-35eb-9069-7589d5849827> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/5b5ff8cd-f2a6-3351-837a-a2d840687790> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Chair seat canvas, embroidered with wool and silk in shades of mustard, red, pink, green, blue, grey, beige, mauve, brown, cream, and yellow.\nThe border has a mustard-coloured ground and is decorated with large, brightly-coloured flowers; carnation, lily, convolvulus and peony.\nThe central embroidered scene of 'The Father and Jupiter' is taken from William Kent's illustration to the 39th of Gay's Fables. The initials 'E.W.' are embroidered on a plinth in the foreground of the scene."@en , "Embroidered chair seat, England, ca. 1730."@en ;
